> syn keyword nhDesConstant
>     \ altar arboreal asleep awake blessed bottom broken burn center chaos
>     \ closed coaligned \contained cursed down dust east engrave false filled
>     \ half-left half-right hardfloor hostile law left levregion lit locked
>     \ mark m_feature m_monster m_object neutral noalign nodoor nommap
>     \ noncoaligned none north noteleport open peaceful random right sanctum
>     \ shortsighted shrine south top true uncursed unfilled unlit up west
> 
> ...when removing the \ from \contained then the two types (keywords and
> string/character constants) will be distinguished. (Tested with Vim 6.4)

But doing that makes vim see the "contained" as an extra definition for
nhDesConstant, not as a keyword for the des-file.  You can see this by
typing ":syntax"; vim lists all those nhDesConstant keywords as contained.
And as nhDesConstants are not defined as contained by something else,
they never get any color applied to them, afaik.

